 ('Reading · A news report',news('Debut Novel About a Lighthouse Keeper Tops Halloran Prize Shortlist',['The judges of the (fictional) Halloran Prize **announced** on Monday a **shortlist of six** novels, **led by** a debut, *The Keeper’s Ledger*, by Anita Soyer. The **panel chair**, critic Marcus Bell, **praised** its “**unhurried**, almost **liturgical** prose,” **adding that** the book “**earns** its slow pace.”','Not everyone **agreed**. A rival publisher **complained** that debuts **receive disproportionate attention**, **while** the prize’s organisers **insisted** that the process is **blind**. The winner **will be named** in November, **and** will receive a **cash award** of £20,000. **Readers can vote** for a **people’s choice** on the prize website.'],kicker='BOOKS NEWS',by='By staff (fictional)',gloss=[('shortlist','lista final de finalistas'),('liturgical','litúrgico'),('blind','às cegas'),('award','prêmio')])),
